{
  "_readme": [
    "Canonical laboratory analytes and how they appear on real reports.",
    "",
    "`aliases` are matched case-insensitively against the label to the left of",
    "a value. The canonical key itself is always matched, so it need not be",
    "repeated. Longest alias wins, so 'total bilirubin' beats 'bilirubin'.",
    "",
    "`unit` is the unit this project stores values in. `unit_aliases` maps the",
    "spellings seen on reports onto it. A value whose unit is present but NOT a",
    "known alias is kept with its original unit and flagged as unconverted —",
    "silently treating mg/dL as g/dL would corrupt the number.",
    "",
    "NOTE ON REFERENCE RANGES: this file deliberately contains none. Normal",
    "ranges vary by laboratory, assay, age and sex. Abnormality is only ever",
    "determined from a range printed on the report itself."
  ],
  "analytes": {
